   "source": [
    "# Apigee Unified AI Gateway — Guided Walkthrough & Policy Lab\n",
    "\n",
    "## Overall Description (What This Notebook Does & Why It Matters)\n",
    "Welcome to the **Apigee Unified AI Gateway** interactive deployment and validation lab!\n",
    "\n",
    "When organizations connect applications to Large Language Models (LLMs) like **Gemini on Vertex AI**, they need more than a raw model endpoint—they need **security, privacy, cost governance, low latency, and executive visibility**.\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook walks you step-by-step through deploying and validating an enterprise-grade **AI Gateway** on Google Cloud Apigee:\n",
    "1. **Unified AI Entrypoint (Area 1):** Connect to Gemini and partner models using the standard OpenAI `/v1/chat/completions` format so applications stay portable across providers.\n",
    "2. **AI Safety Guardrails (Area 2):** Block prompt-injection and jailbreak attacks automatically at the edge with **Google Cloud Model Armor**.\n",
    "3. **Automatic Privacy & PII Redaction (Area 3):** Detect and mask sensitive personal data (emails, phone numbers, SSNs, credit cards) in real time with **Cloud Sensitive Data Protection (SDP)**.\n",
    "4. **Access Control & Token Cost Budgets (Area 4):** Enforce API key authentication, per-product model allow-lists, and **API Product token quotas**—dynamically resolving the active key's API Product limits so both the LLM response and the gateway UI report exact token budgets alongside realistic FinOps workload and auto-burst (`200 OK` → `HTTP 429`) tests.\n",
    "5. **Semantic Caching for Speed & Savings (Area 5):** Serve instant responses for semantically similar questions—slashing latency and reducing LLM token cost to zero on cache hits.\n",
    "6. **Executive Business & FinOps Observability (Area 6):** Deploy Apigee custom AI analytics reports (`./reports/create-reports.sh`) and render a 4-panel Executive Governance & FinOps Dashboard.\n",
    "7. **Resource Inventory & Safe Cleanup (Area 7):** Audit all deployed gateway resources and optionally undeploy lab proxies when done.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "### Step 0 — Preflight Inputs, Dependency Installation & Background Service Account Setup\n",
    "- **What this step does:** Automatically installs and verifies all required dependencies (including **Apigee Templater CLI `aft`**, `gcloud`, `jq`, `git`, `curl`, `requests`, `pyyaml`, and `matplotlib`), clones the gateway template repository, authenticates with Google Cloud, enables required APIs, **automatically creates and configures the runtime Service Account (`apigee-ai-gw@<APIGEE_ORG>.iam.gserviceaccount.com`) in the background**, and resolves your live Apigee gateway hostname—showing a live **⏳ In Progress** tracker at every stage.\n",
    "- **Why it is necessary:** Configures all CLI tools, credentials, IAM bindings (`<GoogleAccessToken>`), and modular deployment/testing helpers in one place so every step in Areas 1–7 executes cleanly with a single click.\n",
    "- **What you need to do (Inputs):** Update the 6 preflight parameters below (set `APIGEE_ORG` to your Google Cloud / Apigee organization ID) and click **Run (▶)**.\n",
    "- **What you will get (Outputs):** A live in-progress status banner while provisioning runs, followed by a green **✅ PASS** Readiness Scorecard confirming `aft`, your Apigee environment, background-provisioned Service Account, and gateway endpoint are ready."
   ]
  },
