   },
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## Area 3 — DLP / PII Detection and Redaction (Sensitive Data Protection)\n",
    "\n",
    "### Business Value\n",
    "Prevents sensitive customer or employee data—such as names, email addresses, phone numbers, Social Security Numbers, and credit card numbers—from leaking to upstream LLMs by automatically de-identifying PII in transit with **Google Cloud Sensitive Data Protection (SDP)**.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Step 3.0 (Optional) — Create SDP Inspect & De-identify Templates\n",
    "- **What this step does:** Automatically creates (or updates if already present) two regional **Cloud Sensitive Data Protection (SDP)** templates in `REGION` from Step 0—one for `SdpInspectTemplateName` (detecting names, emails, phone numbers, US SSNs, and credit card numbers) and one for `SdpDeidentifyTemplateName` (replacing detected PII with infoType tokens such as `[EMAIL_ADDRESS]` and `[CREDIT_CARD_NUMBER]`).\n",
    "- **Why it is necessary (when needed):** Run this optional cell if you do not already have SDP inspect and de-identify templates provisioned in `REGION`. When executed, **Step 3.1** automatically takes the newly created template names and continues without asking. Skip this step if you already have existing SDP templates in `REGION` that you want to enter in Step 3.1.\n",
    "- **What you need to do (Inputs):** Optionally customize `INSPECT_TEMPLATE_ID`, `DEIDENTIFY_TEMPLATE_ID`, or `MIN_LIKELIHOOD`, and click **Run (▶)** (or skip directly to Step 3.1).\n",
    "- **What you will get (Outputs):** A green **✅ PASS** card confirming both SDP templates are ready in `REGION` and registered for automatic handoff to Step 3.1.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Step 3.1 — Undeploy Previous Proxy & Deploy SDP Anonymization Proxy\n",
    "- **What this step does:** Undeploys `llm-gateway-completions-no-auth-model-armor`, resolves `SdpInspectTemplateName` and `SdpDeidentifyTemplateName` in `REGION` (**automatically taking the newly created template names if Step 3.0 was executed, or asking you for the template names if Step 3.0 was skipped**), updates `features/ai-security-anonymization-sdp.yaml`, deploys `templates/llm-gateway-completions-no-auth-ma-sdp.yaml`, and waits until `READY`.\n",
    "- **Why it is necessary:** Layers automatic PII inspection and masking on top of Model Armor safety guardrails.\n",
    "- **What you need to do (Inputs):** Click **Run (▶)**. If you ran Step 3.0, deployment proceeds automatically; otherwise, provide your existing template names in the form fields or when prompted.\n",
    "- **What you will get (Outputs):** A green **✅ PASS** deployment card confirming `llm-gateway-completions-no-auth-ma-sdp` is active.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Step 3.2 — Test Real-Time PII De-identification\n",
    "- **What this step does:** Sends sample customer records containing realistic fake PII and instructs the model to repeat back the exact text it received.\n",
    "- **Why it is necessary:** Visually proves that sensitive fields are redacted before reaching the LLM.\n",
    "- **What you need to do (Inputs):** Select a PII test prompt from `PROMPT` and click **Run (▶)**.\n",
    "- **What you will get (Outputs):** A green **✅ PASS** Web Client card comparing the raw PII prompt sent by the user with the de-identified text seen by the model."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "cell-9b"
   },
   "source": [
    "#@title 3.0 (Optional) Create SDP Inspect & De-identify Templates\n",
    "INSPECT_TEMPLATE_ID = \"ai-gw-sdp-template-inspection\"  #@param {type:\"string\"}\n",
    "DEIDENTIFY_TEMPLATE_ID = \"ai-gw-sdp-template-deidentification\"  #@param {type:\"string\"}\n",
    "MIN_LIKELIHOOD = \"POSSIBLE\"  #@param [\"VERY_UNLIKELY\", \"UNLIKELY\", \"POSSIBLE\", \"LIKELY\", \"VERY_LIKELY\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "target_sdp_loc = REGION\n",
    "inspect_id_clean = INSPECT_TEMPLATE_ID.strip().split(\"/\")[-1].strip()\n",
    "deid_id_clean = DEIDENTIFY_TEMPLATE_ID.strip().split(\"/\")[-1].strip()\n",
    "\n",
    "start_progress(\n",
    "    \"Step 3.0 (Optional) — Provisioning SDP Templates\",\n",
    "    f\"Step 1/2: Creating or updating SDP inspect template '{inspect_id_clean}' in '{target_sdp_loc}'...\",\n",
    ")\n",
    "insp_action, insp_resource = upsert_sdp_inspect_template(inspect_id_clean, target_sdp_loc, MIN_LIKELIHOOD)\n",
    "\n",
    "update_progress(f\"Step 2/2: Creating or updating SDP de-identify template '{deid_id_clean}' in '{target_sdp_loc}'...\")\n",
    "deid_action, deid_resource = upsert_sdp_deidentify_template(deid_id_clean, target_sdp_loc)\n",
    "\n",
    "GATEWAY_STATE[\"sdp_templates\"] = {\n",
    "    \"created\": True,\n",
    "    \"inspect_name\": inspect_id_clean,\n",
    "    \"deidentify_name\": deid_id_clean,\n",
    "    \"location\": target_sdp_loc,\n",
    "}\n",
    "GATEWAY_STATE[\"policy_params\"][\"SdpInspectTemplateName\"] = inspect_id_clean\n",
    "GATEWAY_STATE[\"policy_params\"][\"SdpDeidentifyTemplateName\"] = deid_id_clean\n",
    "\n",
    "infotypes_summary = \", \".join(SDP_DEFAULT_INFOTYPES)\n",
    "show_status_card(\n",
    "    \"PASS\",\n",
    "    \"Step 3.0 Complete — SDP Templates Ready for Step 3.1\",\n",
    "    \"Step 3.1 will automatically use these newly created SDP template names without prompting.\",\n",
    "    rows=[\n",
    "        (\"SdpInspectTemplateName\", f\"{inspect_id_clean} ({insp_action})\"),\n",
    "        (\"Inspect Template Resource\", insp_resource),\n",
    "        (\"SdpDeidentifyTemplateName\", f\"{deid_id_clean} ({deid_action})\"),\n",
    "        (\"De-identify Template Resource\", deid_resource),\n",
    "        (\"SDP Location (Step 0 REGION)\", f\"{target_sdp_loc} (dlp.googleapis.com/v2/projects/{PROJECT_ID}/locations/{target_sdp_loc})\"),\n",
    "        (\"Inspected PII InfoTypes\", f\"{infotypes_summary} (minLikelihood={MIN_LIKELIHOOD})\"),\n",
    "        (\"De-identification Mode\", \"ReplaceWithInfoTypeConfig (e.g. [EMAIL_ADDRESS], [CREDIT_CARD_NUMBER])\"),\n",
    "        (\"Step 3.1 Handoff Status\", \"Auto-configured — click Run (▶) on Step 3.1 to deploy\"),\n",
    "    ],\n",
    ")"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
